msgid "Migrate from OpenTracing to OpenTelemetry tracing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Migrate an application from https://docs.quarkiverse.io/quarkus-smallrye-"
"opentracing/dev/index.html[OpenTracing] to xref:opentelemetry."
"adoc[OpenTelemetry tracing] in Quarkus 3.x."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The legacy OpenTracing framework has been deprecated in favor of the new "
"OpenTelemetry tracing framework. We announced the https://quarkus.io/blog/"
"quarkus-observability-roadmap-2023/#opentracing-archived[OpenTracing "
"deprecation on November 2022], and we are dropping the extension from "
"Quarkus core repository and moving it to the Quarkiverse Hub."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is now time to migrate your application to OpenTelemetry tracing if you "
"haven’t done it yet."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you need to migrate from Quarkus 2.16.x please beware that configuration "
"properties are different and you should check the older Quarkus "
"OpenTelemetry guide version, https://quarkus.io/version/2.16/guides/"
"opentelemetry#configuration-reference[here]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

msgid "To complete this guide, you need:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Roughly 15 minutes"
msgstr ""

msgid "An IDE"
msgstr ""

msgid "JDK 17+ installed with `JAVA_HOME` configured appropriately"
msgstr ""

msgid "Apache Maven {maven-version}"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally the xref:cli-tooling.adoc[Quarkus CLI] if you want to use it"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Optionally Mandrel or GraalVM installed and xref:building-native-image."
"adoc#configuring-graalvm[configured appropriately] if you want to build a "
"native executable (or Docker if you use a native container build)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The demo has 5 parts. Please read the summary and then jump to the section "
"that best fits your use case."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"1 - The *starting point* presents the quickstart app that uses OpenTracing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"2 - The first part is good for anyone performing a *big bang change* of "
"OpenTracing when you don't have any manual instrumentation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"3 - This is the *big bang replacement* of OpenTracing when you have manually "
"instrumented the code. We explain the main differences between OpenTracing "
"and OpenTelemetry"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"4 - The last part uses the *OpenTracing shim*. This is useful if you have a "
"large application with manually instrumented code. It can help performing "
"the migration step by step because it allows the use of the legacy "
"OpenTracing API on top of new OpenTelemetry API"
msgstr ""

msgid "5 - Conclusion and additional resources"
msgstr ""

